# Understanding the Query

The metric

```
process_cpu_usage
```

is exposed by Spring Boot through Micrometer.

It represents the percentage of CPU currently consumed by the running Java process.

Unlike Kubernetes container metrics,

this metric only measures the JVM process itself.

Example

```
Application

↓

Spring Boot

↓

Micrometer

↓

process_cpu_usage

↓

Prometheus

↓

Grafana
```

---

## Why Use avg()

In a Kubernetes deployment,

multiple Pods may be running simultaneously.

Each Pod reports its own CPU utilization.

Example

```
Pod A

22%

Pod B

18%

Pod C

25%
```

Using

```promql
avg(process_cpu_usage{job="auth-service"})
```

produces a single average CPU utilization across all application Pods.

This provides a simplified operational view.

